            alias="matchContexts",
            description='Present only with `matchType: "boolean"`: up to 3 passages showing WHERE this section satisfied the expression (hits in context), in the order they appear in the section. Each highlight is part of what made the section match, judged by the same engine that decides membership: every conjunct of an AND (the first occurrence of each is shown before a second of any), the OR branches that matched, the words of a phrase, both operands of a satisfied `/N`, `/s` or `/p` pair (not the words between them), the occurrences counted by `atleastN`, and for `a NOT W/N b` the `a` that has no `b` in range. A NOT never highlights anything, and neither do words that only occur where they did not take part in the match.\n\nUnlike `excerpt` (the passage the relevance model ranked, which may not contain your terms), these passages always do. Empty (`[]`) when the expression matched only in the heading or citation (`title( )`, `cite( )`). **Absent** on a row whose passages could not be prepared within the search\'s time allowance (a very long section, or a slow read): the row is still a verified match. Contexts never change which sections are returned, their order, or the price.',
