class StatuteSearchRequestChangedSince(RootModel[date_aliased]):
    root: Annotated[
        date_aliased,
        Field(
            description="Only return sections we have OBSERVED change on or after this date (`YYYY-MM-DD`). This is the sync filter: it turns a lookup API into something a nightly job can poll, without creating a board watch per jurisdiction.\n\n**These are observed changes, not effective dates.** A refresh compared the publisher against the copy we held and found it different; the date is when we SAW it, an upper bound on when it took effect. It is the same event stream `GET /us/statutes/section/{actId}/changes` serves per section, so a hit here has a history there.\n\n**Coverage is bounded by capture, not by the age of the law.** Change capture began long after the corpus did, it is per-source, and events are swept at 5 years. An empty result means no captured change in the window, never that nothing was amended.\n\nNarrow with `corpusType` and `state` for a tighter window: the change set is resolved to concrete sections before the search runs, and a window matching too many sections is rejected with a 422 that says so rather than silently truncating your answer.",
            examples=["2026-08-01"],
            title="Changedsince",
        ),
    ]


